# Sentence Case in Headings

Always use sentence case for all headings in documentation, markdown files, and code comments. Only the first word and proper nouns should be capitalized; all other words must be lowercase. Do not use title case except for proper nouns.

Apply this rule to all heading levels (e.g., H1, H2, H3, etc.) and in all documentation formats.

**Example:**
- Good: `## Configure your application`
- Bad: `## Configure Your Application`

This rule ensures consistency and readability across the codebase and documentation.

See also: [technical-writing-style.mdc](mdc:technical-writing-style.mdc) for additional writing guidelines.
